Subject: [PATCH] [mlir] Inline a callee whose block ends in a terminator that does not return

Inlining a single-block callee that ends in ub.unreachable aborts
("must implement handleTerminator in the case of one inlined block"): the
inliner's single-block fast path asks the terminator's dialect to forward
its operands to the call's results, then splices the rest of the caller's
block after the inlined operations. ub.unreachable has nothing to forward,
and nothing may follow it in its block; the ub dialect implements neither
handleTerminator hook. #206083 is the same failure for vector.yield.

- inlineRegionImpl takes the fast path only when the inlined block's
  terminator is ReturnLike; any other single block is inlined as the
  multi-block path does it, the rest of the caller's block moving to a
  block of its own.
- The inliner pass treats a single-block callee whose terminator is not
  ReturnLike as it treats a multi-block callee: not inlined into a region
  that must stay one block.
- UBInlinerInterface implements handleTerminator(Operation *, Block *) as
  a no-op: ub.unreachable stays the terminator of its inlined block, and
  the block after the call has no predecessor from it.

Tests in mlir/test/Dialect/UB/inlining.mlir: a call of a function that
never returns is inlined into a function, and stays a call in an scf.for.
---
 mlir/lib/Dialect/UB/IR/UBOps.cpp            |  5 +++
 mlir/lib/Transforms/Utils/Inliner.cpp       |  9 +++++-
 mlir/lib/Transforms/Utils/InliningUtils.cpp | 13 ++++++--
 mlir/test/Dialect/UB/inlining.mlir          | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mlir/lib/Dialect/UB/IR/UBOps.cpp b/mlir/lib/Dialect/UB/IR/UBOps.cpp
index ee523f9522953db3712e9960eaf8266be612d7ed..d9fb70b2975893f93c380fb25c6accc163853aed 100644
--- a/mlir/lib/Dialect/UB/IR/UBOps.cpp
+++ b/mlir/lib/Dialect/UB/IR/UBOps.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,11 @@ struct UBInlinerInterface : public DialectInlinerInterface {
   bool isLegalToInline(Operation *, Region *, bool, IRMapping &) const final {
     return true;
   }
+
+  /// `ub.unreachable` never returns to the caller: it stays the terminator
+  /// of its inlined block, and nothing branches from it to the block that
+  /// receives the call's results.
+  void handleTerminator(Operation *, Block *) const final {}
 };
 } // namespace
 
